# Code owners.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owner on every pull request that touches a
# matching path. On its own that is a notification, not a control: enforcement
# needs "Require review from Code Owners" in a ruleset, which is deliberately
# not on yet — see the governance note in README.md's CI section for the trigger
# that turns it on (a second contributor, or the repo going public).
#
# It is here now because the file has to exist and be correct *before* the
# ruleset can reference it, and because CI configuration is the one place where
# an unreviewed change can disable every other check in the repository.

# Everything, by default.
*                       @lmvdz

# CI, its gates, and the policy engine that keeps them honest. A change here can
# turn every other check in the repo green without running any of it.
/.github/               @lmvdz
/scripts/ci/            @lmvdz
